WEBVTT

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:08.170
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:08.170
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.470
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:13.470
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:18.850
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:18.850
the only thing I truly have

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:24.140
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:24.140
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:29.480
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:29.480
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.740
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:34.740
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.120
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:40.120
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:46.210
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:46.210
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:51.760
garakuta no yama kara

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:51.760
In the junk I've piled up,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.840
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:55.840
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.140
hibike kono koe yo

00:00:55.840 --> 00:01:01.140
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.400
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:07.400
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:13.070
namida kareru made

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:13.070
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.120
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:18.120
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.450
namida hareru made

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:23.450
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:28.460
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:28.460
though I may lose my way,

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.300
egakikake no ima

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:32.300
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:33.800
kizamu

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:39.550
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:35.090
akashi

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.550
kono te de

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:47.290
Murdoch the Curse is on another streak of failure.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:50.250
Fans are booing the Hornets' five straight losses.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:54.300
I enticed him with some good bonuses...

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.340
That useless idiot!

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.550
And he even injured our golden boy, Keene.

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:03.010
Don't let him play ever again!

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:07.100
The Hornets have no use for someone who can't draw a large crowd.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.150
A Chain of Negativity

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.150
A Chain of Negativity

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.160
I haven't been to L.A. in ages.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:24.330
A two-game series with the Panthers.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:26.910
They're second in the Western Division, right?

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.040
Yeah.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:31.960
They stepped their game up in the second half of the season, and now they're battling the Salmons for first.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.090
Really?

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:37.210
The Coyotes have an overwhelming lead in our division.

00:02:37.210 --> 00:02:39.010
It's nice and peaceful, though.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.970
It isn't nice.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.970
It's no surprise that the Panthers are doing so good.

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:49.230
They dropped the player who sucked in the first half of the season.

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.770
Which guy?

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.940
I see.

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:02.370
Man, I'm full!

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.620
Hey, Shigeno.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.490
What?

00:03:04.490 --> 00:03:06.660
If you're free, wanna go catch a movie?

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.790
There's a really interesting one playing right now.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:11.870
Sorry.

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:13.460
I think I'll pass for today.

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.290
Oh, really?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:16.340
By the way,

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.800
do you know which room Murdoch's in?

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.770
Even if he picked a fight with you,

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:32.480
you don't know if the error was intentional.

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:44.280
Welcome back, Papa!

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.580
Did you buy the cake?

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.490
H-Hello?

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.040
You're the guy who fought with my daddy!

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:58.880
Ow!

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.800
What's wrong, Sandy?

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:06.050
Oh, aren't you...

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.680
Oh, hi.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.760
I'm Shigeno.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.100
Right, Mr. Shigeno.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.890
The pitcher with the fastball.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.690
I'm Connie, Mike's wife.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:16.400
Um, is Murdo—

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.650
Is your husband home?

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:22.280
He just left to buy her birthday cake.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:25.410
Her birthday was actually last week,

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:29.540
but he's been at work with the Indianapolis Hornets,

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.620
so he said that since he's in town for an away game, he'd come home and throw a party.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.960
Um...

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.880
Would you like to wait inside?

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.960
Oh, no.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:42.760
It's nothing important.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:43.670
Bye.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.640
Oh, Mr. Shigeno.

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:50.310
Um...

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:52.600
About the fight that broke out the other day...

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.190
I'm sorry.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:05:00.110
Mike isn't really sociable, and he's a bit impatient.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.230
Oh, don't worry.

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:06.410
He was irritated, and his finger clipped the ball when he tried to throw to first.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:14.210
Yet... he's always misunderstood because he tries to put up a front.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:19.000
If he could get along with people better, he wouldn't be traded all the time.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:23.210
No.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.630
You don't need to apologize.

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:26.430
It was partly my fault.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.800
See ya.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:34.390
Murdoch?

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:35.640
Yes.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.940
The owner wants him off the starting roster immediately.

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.770
W-Wait a minute.

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:44.740
With Keene injured, we're already down a good batter.

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.200
We can't take a power hitter like Murdoch out of the lineup.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:50.990
You've been losing <i>because</i> he hasn't been hitting.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.660
W-Well, yes...

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.580
But—

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.410
I'm simply relaying the owner's instructions.

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.790
You can make your own call,

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:06.050
but please don't forget that this season, your job is on the line.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:15.310
I'm back.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:17.850
Welcome back.

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.520
Did you buy the chocolate cake?

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.610
Yeah!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.570
All right!

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:24.400
I love you, Papa!

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:30.820
Okay Missy, shall we have cake now?

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:32.830
But what should you do before that?

00:06:32.830 --> 00:06:35.290
Yeah, I'll wash my hands.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.660
Good girl.

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.210
Cake! Cake!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.630
Oh, Mr. Shigeno stopped by not too long ago.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.420
What? Shigeno?

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:46.670
That son of a...

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.670
Did he come here to complain again?

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:50.890
No.

00:06:50.890 --> 00:06:53.260
He came to say that he was also at fault for what happened.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.640
That's all.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:09.900
He has the power.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:14.240
I think he'll gain momentum if he shows some results in this series.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.030
Now hitting, number 33:

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.910
Murdoch!

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.390
Oh, he's gonna blow it again!

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.100
How about you do your job, you good-for-nothing!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:41.730
Play!

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:45.020
Come on! Get a hit!

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:52.740
Out!

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.200
Out!

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:01.870
Double play, and the game is over!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.710
That's the sixth straight loss for the Hornets!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:08.130
They're six games behind the first-place team.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.130
This can't get any worse.

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.810
Man, it's one heck of a curse.

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:24.730
Yeah.

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:28.820
We've been shaky ever since he came along.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:31.240
It already hurts that Keene can't play,

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:35.950
and the very cause of that can't do anything either.

00:08:35.950 --> 00:08:37.280
Man...

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.250
The season's going to end with pointless games again.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:42.330
Hey!

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.370
Don't blame everything on Murdoch.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:46.000
Watts.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.460
He isn't the only one who hasn't gotten a hit in the last six games,

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.010
and the pitchers have allowed runs too.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.970
It's everyone's responsibility.

00:08:53.970 --> 00:09:00.060
Yeah, but the team's mood has definitely gotten worse ever since he came.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.100
He's also unsociable.

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:06.270
I'm saying that you should stop blaming someone with a stupid excuse like curses!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.740
What's Watts' problem?{lol, just laughed when I read this line out loud}

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:23.500
Why is he taking Murdoch's side?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.790
No, Watts is totally right.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:30.840
And the season's not even close to over.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:33.210
Look who's making the mood worse

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:39.140
by saying how we're finished, or how playing games is pointless.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:50.860
I'll be starting tomorrow.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.940
We didn't start losing only when Murdoch joined.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.110
I started this series of losses.

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.280
I'll put an end to it.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.200
Murdoch.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:03.330
I've been patient with you this past week,

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.580
but our circumstances are rather grave.

00:10:06.080 --> 00:10:06.830
And?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:10.750
The next game will be your last chance.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:13.130
If you can't show me anything good tomorrow,

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.760
I'll have to ask you to sit in the dugout.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.220
Got it?

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:21.550
Is that all right, Murdoch?

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:24.310
Okay.

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.480
Why?!

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.610
It's more than obvious that he's not doing well!

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.860
Why did you give him another chance?

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:40.410
You're being too soft on him.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:44.160
If you continue to ignore the owner's instructions, you're going to lose your...

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:50.040
Tony, do you remember Shigeno's pitching in the first game of the season's second half?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.330
Y-Yes.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:54.380
Of course I do.

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:56.300
It was amazing.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:59.050
That's when he came down with the yips.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.930
I thought I'd misjudged him.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.720
I thought he'd just gotten lucky at the World Cup,

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:09.390
and in reality, was a rookie who couldn't take the pressure.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:11.850
But he wasn't.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.520
Unbelievably, he came back.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:20.990
And the team continued to win, inspired by his fighting spirit.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:24.990
The Hornets are trying to be born anew.

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:29.660
So you're saying Murdoch will change like Shigeno.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.540
But he's—

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.290
I know.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.710
Yes, Murdoch does cause some problems.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:41.800
However, he's been swinging his bat in the majors for ten years, even though he's been traded over and over again.

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:45.220
I want to take one more bet on his stubbornness.

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:50.560
You better be kidding me.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:02.650
Shigeno.

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:03.450
Yo.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:12.750
So, what is it?

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.790
You wanted to ask me something?

00:12:14.790 --> 00:12:18.340
Say, why do you look out for Murdoch?

00:12:19.460 --> 00:12:21.340
Oh, no.

00:12:21.340 --> 00:12:25.550
I don't think all the losses are his fault either,

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:28.640
but he's not really someone people need to look out for.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:32.850
Yeah, he isn't.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:36.620
But there's a reason he's like that.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:44.320
Murdoch and I used to be on St. Louis' minor team when we were young.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:50.080
He was always short-tempered,

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:53.960
but he was still bright and sociable back then.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:58.670
He made the starting roster and began to show good results...

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:02.090
until a certain incident.

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:08.180
Two people tested positive for cocaine during a surprise drug test.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:14.520
Cocaine was also found in Murdoch's locker, and he was arrested.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:19.110
However, Murdoch was innocent.

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:26.150
The other two had hidden cocaine in his locker to get lighter sentences.

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:33.660
Later on, their confessions proved his innocence.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:34.080
But...

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:41.420
none of his teammates believed him when he claimed his innocence.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:43.920
Including me.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.850
Ever since then, he's stopped believing in anyone.

00:13:49.850 --> 00:13:55.390
"Fighting for the team," or "Winning as a team"

00:13:55.390 --> 00:13:59.190
are probably nothing more than words to him.{meaning words, and no real feelings/trust/etc to it}

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:02.940
Papa.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.990
Sandy.

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.660
It was a close game today, wasn't it?

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:14.950
I'm sorry, Sandy.

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:19.250
I wanted to hit a home run for your birthday.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:21.170
No, it's okay.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.510
If you want anything, just tell me.

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:26.880
I'll get you anything.

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:32.510
I want to see your team be the best, Papa.{lit: win the championships}

00:14:34.180 --> 00:14:40.350
I want to see you be the best, and smile on the baseball field.

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.830
Try saying that again!{why the fuck are these guys out here?}

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.410
Sure, I'll say it again.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.000
Your dad's completely useless.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:03.130
It's no wonder The Curse got chased out of the Panthers.

00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:03.920
Yeah!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:08.670
He's The Curse no matter where he is, so he'll get chased out of the Hornets too!

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:09.800
No he's not!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.470
My daddy's not a curse!

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.050
You...

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:15.640
Now you've done it!

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:16.850
Take this!

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:19.940
You sure are brave for being a child of The Curse!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:20.890
Well look at this!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.810
You sure got a lot of energy this early in the day.

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:27.110
If you want to move around so much, why don't we play some baseball?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:30.070
Hey, let's get out of here.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:30.900
Yeah.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:37.870
Getting in a fight?

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:39.960
No.

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:42.460
It's none of your business.

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.580
I used to fight all the time.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:48.550
My dad was a baseball player too.

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:53.260
I fought with anyone who made fun of him, no matter how big they were.

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.890
I always just ended up with bruises though.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.480
My daddy's hit at least fifteen home runs on every team he's played for.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.940
And I literally mean "always"!

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:10.860
Really, that's amazing.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:14.870
But my daddy always goes to teams with weak hitting.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:20.660
When the team starts to get stronger, he always gets in a fight and quits.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.960
I probably won't be able to see him be the best this year again...

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.460
Sure you can.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:34.590
Your daddy's gonna turn the Hornets into the best.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.260
If you don't believe in him, who will?

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.470
Right!

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:44.480
While you're at it, cheer for Mr. Goro too.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:45.730
"Goro"?

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.610
You have such a weird name!

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:48.820
Say what?

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:54.490
The hit goes deep into left field.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:55.360
All right!

00:16:56.070 --> 00:16:58.620
Roy runs straight home from first.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.580
No, he stops at third.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:02.870
Dunstan slides into second.

00:17:02.870 --> 00:17:07.330
Dunstan, batting third in place of Keene, hasn't let us down.

00:17:07.330 --> 00:17:10.670
With one out and two runners on base, the Hornets have a chance to score.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:14.650
Now hitting, number 11: Parker!

00:17:20.600 --> 00:17:21.890
A walk...

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.310
It's the first inning, and they're loading the bases.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:27.190
Murdoch's old teammates are making a fool out of him.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:28.190
Yeah.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:30.570
Ball!

00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:31.610
Ball four!

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.970
Now hitting, number 33:

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.680
Murdoch!

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.160
Papa!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.580
Do your best!

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:47.000
Sorry, Murdoch.

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:52.420
You used to play with us, so we know how much you suck under pressure.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:55.720
Every single one of them is looking down on me.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:01.300
My teammates talk behind my back, saying I'm some stupid curse.

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:07.060
The coaches want to make me a scapegoat for their failure to take the league title.

00:18:07.700 --> 00:18:08.690
Strike!

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:13.110
Give me a break.

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:17.030
This team's just like every other team.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:18.740
I don't need you to kick me out!

00:18:18.740 --> 00:18:20.160
I'll...

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.700
leave this team on my own!

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:28.370
I want to see your team be the best, Papa.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:33.550
Out!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.170
Out!

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.140
Damn it!

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:43.560
Papa...

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.140
My, my...

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:47.140
Can't he even hit a decent fly?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:52.690
It's the bottom of the first, and Shigeno takes the mound for the Hornets.

00:18:52.690 --> 00:18:54.860
The Hornets can't afford another loss.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.280
Will Shigeno be able to bring the team a win?

00:18:58.280 --> 00:18:59.360
Play!

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.160
We still have more than thirty games to play.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.290
Six games aren't worth giving up on.

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:13.080
I'll blow away this stupid mood...

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:14.590
like it's nothing!

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:18.300
Strike!

00:19:19.990 --> 00:19:21.970
I-It's fast...

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.140
Strike out!

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:29.100
Strike out!

00:19:33.520 --> 00:19:36.190
Strike out!

00:19:40.360 --> 00:19:43.620
Th-Three batters, three outs.

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:44.490
Yeah.

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.620
Wow.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:51.960
Hey, what?

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:55.710
He's going all out from the first inning.

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:58.250
I don't think he cares about lasting till the end.

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:04.470
He's just telling his entire team not to give up yet.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:10.060
The game's entering the sixth, with no runs by either team.

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:15.610
With one out, and a runner on second for the Hornets, Murdoch is at bat.

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.480
The count is 3-2, and here comes the seventh pitch.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:21.860
Strike out!

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.200
Wh-What?

00:20:26.490 --> 00:20:28.990
Come on, you call that a strike?

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:31.620
Want me to introduce you to a good optometrist?

00:20:31.620 --> 00:20:33.670
Or do you just need to buy some glasses?

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.540
Well, how is it?

00:20:35.540 --> 00:20:37.500
Hey, stop, Murdoch!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:41.720
Umpire, wasn't that a little strict?

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.300
It was low.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.470
Don't you think it was a ball?

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.470
My goodness.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:47.970
Now he's picking a fight with the umpire.

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.310
Damn it!

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:58.650
Out!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.190
Three outs!

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:02.530
Still no runs for the Hornets.

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:04.360
The game continues with no runs for either team.

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:07.530
Shigeno walks up to the mound yet again.

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:12.200
His pitching's been fantastic, allowing just one infield hit, and one walk.

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:15.580
Shigeno is putting up a mighty fight on his own, with no help from the batters.

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:17.380
Play!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.420
Oops.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:24.220
Safe! Safe!

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:29.180
My error?

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.720
Are you serious?

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:36.900
Is my fielding percentage gonna go down because he sucks?

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:38.900
I can't do this.

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:42.400
Hey, come over here for a second!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:46.280
Why did you just shrug?

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.410
Again?

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.410
You're the one who can't throw well!

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:51.530
And you're blaming me?

00:21:51.530 --> 00:21:53.660
You...

00:21:53.660 --> 00:21:56.120
What about it?

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.210
Give it a break, Murdoch.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:01.250
You don't believe in anyone.

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:05.920
So stop getting pissed off about every little thing.

00:22:07.010 --> 00:22:10.720
It's not like you have to trust your teammates.

00:22:10.720 --> 00:22:11.600
But let me tell you this:

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:16.020
If you're a professional, complain <i>after</i> you've proven yourself to your teammates!

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:21.560
Your opponent isn't a teammate, the umpire, or the coaches, old man!

00:22:23.020 --> 00:22:24.570
You son of a...!

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.490
Papa!

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:59.460
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:59.460
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:04.820
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.460 --> 00:23:04.820
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:11.080
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:05.200 --> 00:23:11.080
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:15.870
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:15.870
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:22.500
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:22.500
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:28.340
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:28.340
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:34.180
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:34.180
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:39.600
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:39.600
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:46.070
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:46.070
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:51.320
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:54.790
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:51.320 --> 00:23:54.790
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.790 --> 00:23:57.250
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.790 --> 00:24:03.630
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:57.250 --> 00:24:03.630
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:07.470
sotto

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:07.470
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:15.660
Preview

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:15.660
Preview

00:24:11.510 --> 00:24:13.340
Guys, don't give up yet.

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:17.760
If we win this game, we can still battle for first place.

00:24:17.760 --> 00:24:21.230
Hey, are you sure you understand, old man Murdoch?!

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:25.310
Next time, on Major: The Responsibility of an Ace.

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:27.980
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:31.120
Next Time

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:31.120
Next Time

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:31.120
The Responsibility of an Ace

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:31.120
The Responsibility of an Ace
